{"org":"elastic","repo":"elasticsearch","prNumber":"113272","commit":"f93cf80dc1d131dbaf65ea1876f76c908bf3c65b","generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"The `addSuppliers` method in `#PBD1R` adds suppliers for single and multiple rows based on the provided `minRows` and `maxRows`. However, it does not handle cases where `minRows` is greater than 1. If `minRows` is greater than 1, it should add a supplier that generates lists with at least `minRows` elements.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/MultiRowTestCaseSupplier.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/MultiRowTestCaseSupplier.java--15075:15684","promptId":"#PBD1R","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/MultiRowTestCaseSupplier.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/MultiRowTestCaseSupplier.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":15075,"endPos":15684,"startLine":434,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":451,"endLineOffset":5,"length":610}]}]},{"comment":"The `assertTestCaseResultAndWarnings` method uses `assert testCase.getMatcher().matches(Double.NaN) \u003d\u003d false;` and similar checks for positive and negative infinity. These checks are redundant because the subsequent `assertThat(result, not(equalTo(Double.NaN)));` and similar assertions already cover these cases. The matcher should be used to assert the expected result directly without additional checks for specific values.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/AbstractFunctionTestCase.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/AbstractFunctionTestCase.java--33695:34748","promptId":"#9CT4X","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/AbstractFunctionTestCase.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/